  "domain": "infrastructure",
  "definition": "A Bode Plot is a pair of frequency-domain graphs used in control engineering and signal analysis to characterise the frequency response of a linear time-invariant system: one graph plots the magnitude of the system's transfer function in decibels against log-frequency, and the second plots the phase angle in degrees against log-frequency. Together they reveal gain margins, phase margins, bandwidth, and resonant behaviour, making Bode plots the primary graphical tool for assessing open-loop stability and designing compensators.",
